  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "The study analyzes young people's experiences with electrical infrastructures and power outages using mixed qualitative and quantitative data. It tracks the physical and material ways youth notice, feel, and adapt to routine electricity disruptions in their daily lives.",
      "why": "It establishes electrical outages as a defining feature of youth geography, bridging a gap between energy infrastructure research and childhood studies."
    }
